  "start": 0.0,
  "end": 21.72,
  "titre": "Le scandale énergétique choquant",
  "citation": "Good evening. Tonight we look at the energy crisis in Europe, and what it means for ordinary families. Prices for gas have tripled in two years. Many governments promised help, but the help arrived late, and it went mostly to large companies. That is the first scandal nobody talks about. Let me give you the numbers."
 },
 "passages": [
  {
   "n": 1,
   "start": 68.34,
   "end": 92.7,
   "titre": "Contrats secrets et réseaux non prêts",
   "citation": "There is a second issue. The new contracts signed with foreign suppliers are secret. Parliament was not allowed to read them. Members of Parliament asked, and they were told it was a matter of national security. National security for a gas contract. Finally, the transition. Leaders promise green energy, cheap and clean. But the grids are not ready.",
   "annonce": "Dans ce segment, on va découvrir un point crucial : les contrats secrets avec les fournisseurs étrangers et les promesses non tenues sur les réseaux verts."
  }
 ],
